<article class="env-lemma" id="084G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/084G">Lemma <span data-tag="084G">71.11.8</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0849" data-tag="0849">71.11.1</a>. If $\mathcal{A}$ is of finite type as a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-algebras, then $\pi : \underline{\text{Proj}}_ X(\mathcal{A}) \to X$ is of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/040Y" data-tag="040Y">67.23.4</a> and the construction of the relative Proj this follows from the case of schemes which is Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZY" data-tag="07ZY">31.31.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>